Sends row 1 of `docs/manual/LANGUAGE.md`'s exit-code table to zero: a `mutate` whose
baseline `verify` came back `violated`/`reachable_failed`/`unknown_cti`/
`unknown_budget` exits 0 while its envelope still reports the failure. A gate
reading only the exit code sees a pass. This is #554 itself. Since #1002 the
same row also carries `refinement_failed`/`impl_violated`, so the mutation now
sends a failed inline `implements` seam to zero as well. Since #901 the row
lives in one place, `outcome::Verdict::exit_code`, which `exit_status`,
the nested refinement fold, the verify-cache replay and `chain` all read, so
the fault reaches every one of them at once.

--- a/rust/fslc/src/outcome.rs
+++ b/rust/fslc/src/outcome.rs
@@ -690,7 +690,7 @@ impl Verdict {
             | Self::UnknownBudget
             | Self::RefinementFailed
             | Self::ImplViolated
-            | Self::Indeterminate => FAILURE_EXIT,
+            | Self::Indeterminate => SUCCESS_EXIT,
             Self::SpecError => SPEC_ERROR_EXIT,
             Self::InternalError => INTERNAL_EXIT,
         }
